# Endovenous radiofrequency or laser ablation of varicose veins (36475, 36476, 36478, 36479), from Medicare LCD L34536
# (WPS). Status draft: awaiting clinical sign-off (vaglio signoff). Every clause is quoted from
# library/sources/L34536-varicose.txt; the codes are those of its billing and coding article A56914.
#
# Drafted by hand. The LCD's indications for any treatment, a failed three-month trial of conservative therapy and
# symptoms (one or more of the six it lists), then those for ablation: the target is the greater or lesser saphenous
# vein or its tributaries, the vein's diameter is within the limit (20 mm for radiofrequency, 30 mm for laser), and none
# of an aneurysm in the target segment, thrombosis or tortuosity that would impair the catheter, or significant
# peripheral arterial disease. Asymptomatic veins, or symptomatic ones without the trial, are cosmetic under the LCD:
# here that is the symptoms or the trial documented absent, which denies. Questions only: the LCD names no codes for
# any of these. Not decided here: sclerotherapy, surgery, mechanochemical (36473, 36474) and adhesive (36482, 36483)
# closure, spider veins, and the duplex scans the LCD allows. States: WPS's jurisdictions 5 and 8; check the
# contractor's current list.
policy varicose_ablation
  title "Endovenous radiofrequency or laser ablation of varicose veins (36475-36479)"
  version 0.1.0
  source "Medicare LCD L34536, Treatment of Varicose Veins of the Lower Extremities (WPS): indications and limitations for ERFA and laser ablation"
  status draft
  authority lcd
  lines medicare-advantage medicare
  states IA KS MO NE IN MI
  questionnaire https://vaglio.example/Questionnaire/varicose-ablation
  service cpt 36475 36476 36478 36479

evidence conservative_failed
  text "A 3-month trial of conservative therapy (exercise, leg elevation, weight loss, graduated compression) has failed"
  clause "A 3-month trial of conservative therapy such as exercise, periodic leg elevation, weight loss, graduated compressive therapy, and avoidance of prolonged immobility where appropriate, has failed, AND"
  find question conservative-failed
  request document loinc 11506-3

evidence symptomatic
  text "Symptoms: pain, aching, cramping, burning, itching or swelling impairing mobility; recurrent superficial phlebitis; a non-healing ulcer; bleeding; stasis dermatitis; or refractory dependent edema"
  clause "The patient is symptomatic and has 1, or more, of the following:"
  find question symptomatic

evidence saphenous_target
  text "The target is the greater or lesser saphenous vein or its tributaries"
  clause "ERFA and laser ablation are covered only for the treatment of symptomatic varicosities of the lesser or greater saphenous veins and their tributaries which have failed 3 months of conservative therapy."
  find question saphenous-target

evidence diameter_within_limit
  text "The vein's maximum diameter is within 20 mm (radiofrequency) or 30 mm (laser)"
  clause "Maximum vein diameter of 20 mm for ERFA or 30 mm for laser ablation."
  find question diameter-within-limit
  request document loinc 18748-4

evidence aneurysm
  text "An aneurysm in the target segment"
  clause "Absence of aneurysm in the target segment."
  find question aneurysm

evidence thrombosis_tortuosity
  text "Thrombosis or vein tortuosity that would impair catheter advancement"
  clause "Absence of thrombosis or vein tortuosity, which would impair catheter advancement."
  find question thrombosis-tortuosity

evidence arterial_disease
  text "Significant peripheral arterial disease"
  clause "The absence of significant peripheral arterial diseases."
  find question arterial-disease

criterion no_trial
  text "A failed 3-month trial of conservative therapy is not documented."
  clause "A 3-month trial of conservative therapy such as exercise, periodic leg elevation, weight loss, graduated compressive therapy, and avoidance of prolonged immobility where appropriate, has failed, AND"
  defeated by conservative_failed

criterion no_symptoms
  text "Symptoms of the kinds the LCD lists are not documented."
  clause "The patient is symptomatic and has 1, or more, of the following:"
  defeated by symptomatic

criterion not_saphenous
  text "A saphenous target is not documented."
  clause "ERFA and laser ablation are covered only for the treatment of symptomatic varicosities of the lesser or greater saphenous veins and their tributaries which have failed 3 months of conservative therapy."
  defeated by saphenous_target

criterion diameter_unshown
  text "A vein diameter within the limit is not documented."
  clause "Maximum vein diameter of 20 mm for ERFA or 30 mm for laser ablation."
  defeated by diameter_within_limit

criterion criteria_met
  text "The trial, symptom, target and diameter requirements are met."
  clause "In addition to the above (see A), the patient's anatomy and clinical condition are amenable to the proposed treatment including ALL of the following:"
  defeated by no_trial no_symptoms not_saphenous diameter_unshown

criterion no_exclusion_shown
  text "No aneurysm, no thrombosis or tortuosity, and no significant arterial disease."
  clause "In addition to the above (see A), the patient's anatomy and clinical condition are amenable to the proposed treatment including ALL of the following:"
  defeated by aneurysm thrombosis_tortuosity arterial_disease

decision approve approves
  text "Approve the ablation."
  clause "ERFA and laser ablation are covered only for the treatment of symptomatic varicosities of the lesser or greater saphenous veins and their tributaries which have failed 3 months of conservative therapy."
  defeated by no_trial no_symptoms not_saphenous diameter_unshown aneurysm thrombosis_tortuosity arterial_disease

decision deny_criteria denies
  text "Deny: the conservative trial, symptoms, saphenous target or diameter requirement is not met."
  clause "The treatment of asymptomatic varicose veins, or symptomatic varicose veins without a 3-month trial of conservative measures, by any technique, will be considered cosmetic and therefore not covered."
  defeated by criteria_met

decision deny_anatomy denies
  text "Deny: an aneurysm, thrombosis or tortuosity, or significant arterial disease makes the anatomy unsuitable."
  clause "In addition to the above (see A), the patient's anatomy and clinical condition are amenable to the proposed treatment including ALL of the following:"
  defeated by no_exclusion_shown
